\section{Problem Definition}
\label{sec:mining-problem}

The subnet selected for this implementation is \textbf{Subnet 32 — itsAI}~[38].
The subnet's incentive mechanism is built around a single, well-defined task:
\textbf{AI-generated text detection}. Miners are rewarded for producing models
capable of accurately distinguishing text written by a human from text
generated by a large language model, and, where possible, classifying which
underlying source produced it.\\[0.3cm]

This task was chosen deliberately as a case study for this thesis, since it
satisfies the core requirement for a well-functioning Bittensor subnet
discussed in Section~\ref{chap:subnets}: the output is objectively measurable
(a text sample either is or is not AI-generated), which makes it possible for
validators to score miner submissions with a clear, non-ambiguous ground
truth.
