\subsection*{Handling Missing Values}
Missing values in the \texttt{source} column were relabelled as an explicit
\texttt{unknown} class rather than discarded, preserving the full dataset
while still allowing \texttt{source} to be used as an auxiliary feature.

\subsection*{Label Construction}
Since the raw dataset stores human and ChatGPT answers in separate columns,
the data was flattened into a long format with a single unified \texttt{Y}
(label) column, alongside the corresponding \texttt{X} (text) column — the
standard supervised-learning shape required for classification.

