\subsection*{Raw-Text Feature Engineering}
~[41]Before embedding the text, a deliberate decision was made to first extract
raw, human-interpretable statistics from it. Embeddings compress text into a
geometric representation that is excellent for similarity and clustering, but
which hides diagnostic signals that are useful during EDA and model
debugging. The following features were engineered directly from the raw
text, grouped by class (AI vs.\ human):

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Word count} per answer
  \item \textbf{Average word length} per answer
  \item \textbf{Character count} per answer
  \item \textbf{Duplicate / near-duplicate detection}, since HC3 is known to
        contain repeated questions across its splits
  \item \textbf{Vocabulary and style statistics}, including average sentence
        length and punctuation frequency
\end{itemize}

These statistics were retained as standalone tabular features and later used
both for standalone classical models and as auxiliary inputs alongside
embeddings.

